hifiberry-analog-recognition (0.4.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Playback state has a single writer again. Recognition reported "playing"
    to AudioControl directly, alongside the state task that owns play/stop.
    That task only re-sends when its own view changes, so a record quiet
    enough to be recognized without crossing the activation level left the
    player reported as playing with nothing that would ever clear it.
    Recognition now signals the state machine, which takes it as evidence of
    playback and applies the usual stop debounce on top.
  * A capture that stops delivering no longer freezes the level. The PipeWire
    process callback can stop firing while the main loop runs on quite
    happily -- a daemon restart, a torn-down link, the target node going away
    -- which left the last measured level latched indefinitely, and a loud one
    held the player in Playing. Levels now carry the time they were measured
    and read as silence once they are more than two seconds old.
  * AudioControl requests now time out. They are awaited on every level tick
    and reqwest applies no timeout of its own, so a server that accepted the
    connection and then went quiet stalled playback detection for good.
  * Reject settings that cannot mean anything. A non-finite activation level
    ("nan" and "inf" both parse as numbers) compared false against every
    level, silently pinning the detector to one state; a negative hysteresis
    put the stop threshold above the start threshold, leaving a band of levels
    that both started and stopped playback once per debounce cycle.
  * setting_poll_secs = 0 no longer takes the service down on its first tick.
    It is clamped to a second -- 0 reads like "off" because for
    stream_check_secs that is exactly what it means.
  * README: document capture_target, threshold_dbfs and hysteresis_db. It
    still described start_threshold and stop_threshold on a -60dB scale,
    neither of which has existed since 0.4.0.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 21:03:44 +0000

